{
  "_comment": [
    "Two sets of shared test vectors, each read by both languages.",
    "",
    "`cases` pins FromTitle (title→session name). Only Go reads it now:",
    "slug/slug_test.go. The browser stopped deriving names with ADR-0019, so",
    "t3-bridge is the caller FromTitle still serves.",
    "An empty want means the title yields nothing usable and the caller supplies",
    "its own fallback (session-N in the lobby, 'claude' in t3-bridge).",
    "",
    "`cleanTitleCases` pins CleanTitle, which has TWO implementations that must",
    "agree: Go's slug.CleanTitle, which tmux-api runs on every title that reaches",
    "it, and frontend-v2/src/lib/title.ts, which the browser runs to show what was",
    "typed. Read by slug/slug_test.go and frontend-v2/test/title.test.ts. The two",
    "disagreeing makes a card change under the person who just retitled it.",
    "",
    "Add a case here rather than to either language's test file."
  ],
  "cleanTitleCases": [
    { "in": "Deploy the thing", "want": "Deploy the thing" },
    { "in": "  padded  ", "want": "padded" },
    { "in": "collapses   inner   runs", "want": "collapses inner runs" },
    { "in": "tab\tand\nnewline", "want": "tab and newline" },
    { "in": "bell\u0007and\u001bescape", "want": "bell and escape" },
    { "in": "c1\u0085control", "want": "c1 control" },
    { "in": "", "want": "" },
    { "in": "   ", "want": "" },
    { "in": "кирилица остава", "want": "кирилица остава" },
    { "in": "emoji 🚀 stays", "want": "emoji 🚀 stays" },
    { "in": "pipe | stays", "want": "pipe | stays" }
  ],
  "cases": [
